# WebRectangle environment configuration
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL. The site runs correctly with no .env file at
# all: discovery works against seed data, and every form still captures and
# confirms. Setting a variable upgrades a capability; leaving it unset never
# breaks one.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in your hosting provider.
# Validated by lib/env.ts at build time, so a malformed value fails loudly and
# early rather than at 2am in a request handler.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canonical origin. Used for metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap and OG images.
# Get this wrong and search engines will index the wrong hostname.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://webrectangle.com"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# THIS SINGLE VARIABLE IS THE ENTIRE "GO TO A REAL BACKEND" SWITCH.
#
# Unset, the app uses the in-memory adapter backed by content/seed/creators.json.
# Set, lib/repositories/index.ts resolves to the Prisma adapter instead, with no
# component, page or Server Action changes.
#
# To activate:
#   1. npm install @prisma/client
#   2. set DATABASE_URL below
#   3. npx prisma migrate dev
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/webrectangle"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lead notifications  (optional, cascading)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# lib/services/notify.ts tries each configured channel and always falls back to
# a server log, so a submission is never silently dropped. With none of these
# set, leads still appear in .data/leads.jsonl during development and in the
# server log in production, and the UI offers a WhatsApp handoff.

# Transactional email via Resend. BOTH must be set for email to activate.
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
# LEAD_NOTIFY_EMAIL="hello@webrectangle.com"

# Slack incoming webhook. Useful as a fast second channel alongside email.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL="https://hooks.slack.com/services/..."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spam protection  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A honeypot field and a submit-timing check are always active and need no
# configuration. Turnstile is an additional layer for when those stop being
# enough. BOTH keys must be set for it to activate.

# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="0x..."
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="0x..."

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Plausible is cookieless and aggregate, which is why no consent banner ships
# with this site. If you swap in a provider that sets cookies, you must add one.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN="webrectangle.com"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduling  (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Cal.com username or team/event slug. When unset, the "book a call" section on
# /contact is omitted entirely rather than rendering a dead link.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_LINK="webrectangle/intro"
